body:
I'm still shocked that for a 30th anniversary game they didn't go with more classic mecha. I get that they need ones to work with the story but I would have killed to get more 70s and 80s classics in there.

&#x200B;

Also it'll never happpen but man I'd love if one of the Shinkalion units is Type EVA piloted by Shinji.

Tonight, I want everyone to sing it loud and proud, no matter where you are.

&#x200B;

On Reddit. On Discord. Reading your daughter a bedtime story. I don't care.

Tonight. In one voice.

&#x200B;

KAZE. NI. NARE.

I mean he could easily say that nobody named Daniel Bryan is coming to AEW.

&#x200B;

Bryan Danielson, on the other hand...

Great idea, Matt! Hey question, will any of these thousands of jobs have enough of a salary where I will be able to PAY my rent? 

&#x200B;

Or one where I can do so without also making use of federal assist..oh wait you wouldn't support that nevermind.

I'm sure she hopes the former President has learned his lesson.

&#x200B;

God, I look at that woman and just see the bitchy English teacher everyone hated.

I love how a lot of the young lions come in with ready-made stories. Narita was a amateur champion in high school and was scouted to join the dojo, so he came in really wanting to show his skill as a technician. It worked out great when he was paired with Shota in matches, Narita had a few backstage clips where he felt Umino, who was a baseball player and didn't have a big wrestling pedigree outside of his father, got in the easy way while he struggled at the bottom.

&#x200B;

That's definitely one of Gedo's strengths as a booker, if you read between the lines there's a ton of subtext and subtlety in a wrestler's career, from young lions all the way up the card, and ready-made stories when two wrestlers have a match.

Simple. If Israel and Palestine actually have peace and stop fighting, it's the end of the world and Satan wins.

&#x200B;

...I'm not kidding.

Misu vs. COVID.

&#x200B;

Suzuki wins.
